  "brief": "DoorDash is in advanced talks to acquire Instacart for $17 billion, while Intel is acquiring Israeli quantum computing startup Classiq for $2.3 billion, and Brookfield is in a take-private deal worth $5.2B with LXP.\n\nDoorDash / Instacart (Rumored): DoorDash and Instacart Deal Rumors. DoorDash is in advanced talks to acquire Instacart for $17 billion [2, 3, 4]. The deal is reportedly valued around $17 billion [3, 6]. The acquisition would involve winding down Caper Carts business [1].\nIntel / Classiq (Announced): Intel Acquires Classiq. Intel is acquiring Israeli quantum computing startup Classiq [12, 13, 14]. The deal is worth $2.3 billion [12, 13, 14]. The acquisition would set a record for a quantum computing deal [14, 16]. The deal was agreed upon for $2.2 billion [17].\nBrookfield / LXP (Pending approval): Brookfield and LXP. Brookfield and LXP are in a take-private deal worth $5.2B [20, 21, 22]. The deal is expected to be completed once approved [23]. The deal's status is currently pending approval [22].\nAres Capital / MidCap Financial Investment (Announced): Ares Capital to Acquire MidCap Financial. Ares Capital is acquiring MidCap Financial Investment for $2.6 billion [24, 25]. The deal was announced on October 27 [24, 25]. No further information is available [24, 25].\nTata Motors / Iveco (Announced): Tata Motors and Iveco Deal. Tata Motors is acquiring Iveco [28, 29, 30]. The deal has cleared the 80% acceptance threshold [26, 27, 31]. The deal is expected to proceed after Iveco shareholders approve resolutions [29].\nT3 Defense / KeepZone AI (Announced): T3 Defense to Acquire KeepZone AI. T3 Defense is acquiring KeepZone AI as part of its homeland security expansion [32]. The deal is aimed at enhancing T3 Defense's capabilities in the homeland security sector [32]. No further details on the acquisition have been disclosed [32].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Announced): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is buying Momentum Midstream for $5.5 Billion [33, 34]. The deal has been announced [33]. No further information is available [34].\nCopperPoint / General Indemnity Group (Completed): CopperPoint Acquires General Indemnity Group. CopperPoint has acquired General Indemnity Group [35]. The deal is now completed [35].",
